 - **BBAI logging is now XML-tunable:** BBAI AI-decision logging can now be enabled/disabled and adjusted through **SAS defines**, rather than editing and recompiling the DLL as in base AdvCiv. This is deemed valuable **not only for modders, but also for users** who can now view or generate `BBAI.log` files for review. Note: `LoggingEnabled=1` in `CivilizationIV.ini` is still required for Civ4 to write. This allowed for example to surgically identify and fix the root cause of a city not producing its first settler until ~T90 at normal game speed, which is way too late (`bWarPlan` was too aggressively gating settler production; now it only blocks settler production after early expansion has reached enough cities (inefficient at that point, better switch strategy)). Note: BBAI logs can be very long; for broad raw-log diagnosis, we usually give to an external LLM/AI such as ChatGPT the log file, as it is as of now agentic-token-free analysis (also good to give us a different point of view/review if needed).
 - **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging and head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-and-head-example).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-record log:** added a separate `SASGameRecord_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It notably records high-level run context such as initial map/landmass geography and bonus/yield context, economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, game state, and in-game bonus appearances/disappearances, complementing BBAI logs by recording what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6033+) It also logs autoplay start/end/change rows, explicit player appearance/revival/elimination rows, and compact run-status rows with alive/eliminated players, current winner/victory if any, and top score/power players, so stopped autoplay logs no longer require inferring these from missing snapshots. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6034+) Free-text fields such as city, player, leader, civ, map-script, and log-file names are quoted/escaped, so names with spaces are easier to parse robustly. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6057+) It also notably records compact per-turn exploration, map changes and environmental status, explicit spaceship launches and project-victory progress, and a full final snapshot when the game is won. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6058+) It notably also records war-declaration causes and sponsors, diplomacy memories, progress for all enabled victories, project-victory resets and failures, and compact full-map revelation. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6077+) It notably also further records active mod and DLL-slot identity, research and production overflow, production conversion and lost-production gold, city buildings and pollution, trade unlocks, and compact territory development including routes, improvements, irrigation, and improved/unimproved bonus types, and also names player-wide health/happiness modifier sources and records AI victory-stage strategies and the target's victory context when war is declared. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6091+) It also records `UnitCombat` shares a